# Claude Code Token Optimization Rules
# Optimized for Claude Code CLI and VS Code extension

## Plugin Installation
Install the token-optimizer plugin:
/plugin marketplace add alexgreensh/token-optimizer
/plugin install token-optimizer@alexgreensh-token-optimizer

Enable auto-update:
/plugin → Marketplaces tab → select alexgreensh-token-optimizer → Enable auto-update

## Basic Commands
/token-optimizer          # Run optimization audit
/token-coach             # Get coaching on token usage
/token-optimizer quick   # Quick optimization

## Conversation Management
- Use /compact to compress conversation history
- Clear context between unrelated tasks
- Avoid long back-and-forth conversations

## Prompt Best Practices
- Be direct: "fix this bug" not "I think there might be a bug"
- Use file references: @backend/main.py instead of pasting code
- Request specific changes: "change line 50 to X" not "improve this"
- Avoid explanations: just ask for the code

## Context Optimization
- Only include relevant files in context
- Use .cursorignore to exclude unnecessary files
- Keep system prompts minimal
- Remove redundant information

## Cache Management
- Use prompt caching for repeated operations
- Keep tool definitions compact
- Cache common patterns and snippets

## Session Management
- Use shorter sessions for focused work
- Break large tasks into smaller sessions
- Clear memory between major task switches
